h-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bf2a082c02b3c27d45ff868117cfc76093df14a97262b09ed6e8e103eac55aa3","event_uuid":"b2177b25-d46f-4fc1-b99b-8bdea96ecb9d","position":{"commit_sha":"ec4bb55863237f9eacc5c6fc03ef98b05f92a2eb","position":"1785452278570212001-b2177b25-d46f-4fc1-b99b-8bdea96ecb9d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bd692e4c6d9064fcb9436594527369413f85021f93202ae83bdc51ca0963b049","event_uuid":"50d06b2a-36f7-4f2a-8776-a6210e90bfea","position":{"commit_sha":"d1540aeda7658fd087fe2a94cdcd1bddf7525355","position":"1785452327275183001-50d06b2a-36f7-4f2a-8776-a6210e90bfea"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7f44a1c1b3d09904cc20eae3528439c15a58d54c65798e75313e49832883ae56","event_uuid":"7214b0be-dc81-4a68-b7bc-625682b568e9","position":{"commit_sha":"6a83d4962ddcb09262038a5a3c7eed010b89e09e","position":"1785452340700912001-7214b0be-dc81-4a68-b7bc-625682b568e9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1785451254852570001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"bb87327f-2df4-431e-bcef-ec2b49f418d9","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"d59e-e042-2b94-4b70"}],"description":"# CLOSED — premise disproven by measurement: scaling the verifier's step budget does not help\n\nThis epic was filed on the premise that the completion verifier's flat budgets were too small\nfor a large ticket and should scale with the acceptance-criteria count. **That premise was\ntested and is false.** The epic is closed as disproven rather than decomposed; a correctly\npremised successor will be filed once the mechanism is identified.\n\n## The disproving measurement\n\nTicket `9fd4-a94c-156e-4a56`, closed twice against the same tree, changing only the budget:\n\n| Step budget | Model requests | Wall clock | s/request | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 480 (default) | 240 — hit the ceiling | 780s | 3.25 | none |\n| 960 (2x) | 480 — hit the ceiling | 4,492s (75 min) | 9.36 | none |\n\nDoubling the budget bought **zero** progress toward a verdict and 5.75x the wall clock. A run\nthat merely needed more headroom would have finished somewhere inside the doubled budget;\ninstead it consumed the new ceiling exactly as it consumed the old one. Per-request time also\nnearly tripled, which points at accumulating tool history — each turn re-sends the whole\nconversation — matching the existing caveat in `docs/llm-framework.md` that raising\n`REBAR_LLM_MAX_TOKENS` \"does not repair repeated tool-history growth\".\n\nThe conclusion holds regardless of whether the non-convergence turns out to be a tool-level\nloop or a termination-awareness failure: neither is fixed by a larger budget.\n\n## Findings that SURVIVE the disproof\n\nThese were measured while investigating and remain true. They are recorded here so the\nsuccessor does not re-derive them:\n\n1. A step-budget exhaustion raises `LLMRunnerError` (`runner.py:465`, `raise budget_err from\n   exc`), not `UnretryableOutputError`, so it falls through recovery's\n   `except UnretryableOutputError` (`completion_recovery.py:405`) and reaches no fallback.\n2. The obvious runaway discriminator does not work: `request_limit = ceil(max_iter/2)` vs\n   `tool_calls_limit = max(8, max_iter)` (`runner.py:414-417`), so a one-tool-call-per-turn\n   loop trips the request ceiling FIRST — indistinguishable from careful sequential work.\n3. `_EVIDENCE_CHARS` (12,000 per criterion) vs `_MAX_TOTAL_EVIDENCE_CHARS` (96,000 aggregate)\n   is incoherent above 8 criteria, and the aggregate check runs INSIDE the loop AFTER each\n   billable call, so a 14-criterion ticket pays for all 14 and then fails with no verdict.\n4. Recovery's per-criterion re-send is uncached: the `cache_control` breakpoint is on\n   `system_prompt` (`runner.py:330-338`) but the context travels in `instructions`.\n5. Recovery is a WEAKER oracle than the aggregate path — its finalizer decides `met` from\n   bounded evidence summaries, never raw source — so availability must not be bought by\n   routing more traffic to it.\n6. There is no wall-clock deadline anywhere in the LLM path; `DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_S` is\n   per-request only. The 75-minute run above was not bounded by anything.\n7. `REBAR_LLM_MAX_STEPS` has no upper bound and no validation — `999999999`, `0` and `-5` all\n   resolve through `_llm_int` unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] the premise \"scaling the step budget lets a large ticket verify\" is tested against the\n      motivating ticket at two budgets, and the result recorded above\n- [x] the surviving findings are captured on this ticket so a successor need not re-derive them\n- [x] no work is decomposed from this epic, because the work it proposed would not have fixed\n      the reported problem","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/completion.py","reason":"criteria-scaled step and output budgets"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py","reason":"recovery entry predicate and coherent evidence bounds"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/runner.py","reason":"step-budget signal typing / limits"},{"path":"docs/llm-framework.md","reason":"document the scaled budgets"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"7214b0be-dc81-4a68-b7bc-625682b568e9","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"94b4-059e-a74a-4cf8","ticket_type":"epic","title":"DISPROVEN: scaling the completion verifier's step budget does not make a large ticket verify","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["52386c83-d2aa-4fe8-8b1d-a7b7ce757e76","bb87327f-2df4-431e-bcef-ec2b49f418d9","e3af7613-c5ba-4173-bdc5-69c46b3c4c77","b2177b25-d46f-4fc1-b99b-8bdea96ecb9d","50d06b2a-36f7-4f2a-8776-a6210e90bfea","7214b0be-dc81-4a68-b7bc-625682b568e9"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659635124456001,"uuid":"3237f97a-4a75-47eb-9b52-4b2d378a2311"}